### 4.3 Implementation Strategy

```
Layer 1: Database (RLS policies) — Enforced at query level
  profiles: Employee sees own row; TL sees team; HR/Admin sees all
  payroll_records: Employee sees own; HR/Admin sees all; TL sees NOTHING
  leaves: Employee sees own; TL sees team; HR sees all
  
Layer 2: Frontend (ProtectedRoute) — Prevents page rendering
  <ProtectedRoute allowedRoles={['admin', 'hr']}>
    <HRPayroll />
  </ProtectedRoute>

Layer 3: Component (Role-aware rendering) — Hides UI elements
  {role === 'hr' && <SalaryColumn />}
  
All three layers must agree. RLS is the ultimate enforcer.
```

