## 9. ATTENDANCE MODEL

### 9.1 Current State

```
CURRENT (work_logs table):
  - Employee clocks in via DashboardLayout (1-second interval timer)
  - Clock in creates work_logs row: user_id, clock_in, status='Active', work_location='WFO'|'WFH'
  - Clock out updates: clock_out, status='Completed'
  - WorkLogs.tsx aggregates by day client-side
  - AI Stand-up Polisher appends notes to work_logs.notes
  
PROBLEMS:
  ❌ No UNIQUE constraint per user per day (multiple active shifts possible)
  ❌ No overtime calculation
  ❌ No late-coming / early-leaving tracking
  ❌ No attendance regularization (forgot to clock out)
  ❌ No shift management
  ❌ Hours calculated entirely client-side
  ❌ Global mutable state for clock status (globalClockedIn)
```

### 9.2 Enterprise Attendance Architecture

```
work_sessions (REPLACES work_logs):
  id                UUID PK
  employee_id       UUID FK → profiles(id) NOT NULL
  session_date      DATE NOT NULL
  clock_in          TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL
  clock_out         TIMESTAMPTZ
  work_location     TEXT CHECK (office|remote|hybrid|client_site)
  status            TEXT CHECK (active|completed|regularized|auto_closed)
  total_hours       DECIMAL GENERATED (clock_out - clock_in in hours)
  overtime_hours    DECIMAL DEFAULT 0 (hours beyond 9)
  is_late           BOOLEAN GENERATED (clock_in > expected_start + grace)
  is_early_exit     BOOLEAN GENERATED (clock_out < expected_end - grace)
  notes             TEXT
  regularization_reason TEXT
  regularized_by    UUID FK → profiles(id)
  created_at        TIMESTAMPTZ
  updated_at        TIMESTAMPTZ
  
  UNIQUE(employee_id, session_date) — Prevent duplicate daily entries

attendance_regularization (NEW):
  id                UUID PK
  work_session_id   UUID FK → work_sessions(id) NOT NULL
  employee_id       UUID FK → profiles(id) NOT NULL
  original_clock_in TIMESTAMPTZ
  original_clock_out TIMESTAMPTZ
  requested_clock_in TIMESTAMPTZ
  requested_clock_out TIMESTAMPTZ
  reason            TEXT NOT NULL
  status            TEXT CHECK (pending|approved|rejected)
  approved_by       UUID FK → profiles(id)
  created_at        TIMESTAMPTZ
```

### 9.3 Attendance Business Rules

```
Standard shift: 09:00 - 18:00 (9 hours)
Grace period: 15 minutes
Overtime: Any hours beyond 9h/day (requires manager acknowledgment)
Auto-close: If clock_out missing by 23:59, auto-close at 18:00 with regularization flag
Late threshold: clock_in > 09:15 → is_late = true
Early exit threshold: clock_out < 17:45 → is_early_exit = true
Monthly attendance report: Aggregated from work_sessions, cross-referenced with leave_requests + holidays
```

